<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Callixtus III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1378">1378</a>–<a href="/years/1458">1458</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Alfons de Borja · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-borgia">House of Borgia</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Callixtus III, born Alfons de Borja near Xàtiva in the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, was pope from 1455 to 1458, the first of the Borgia popes. Formerly an adviser to Alfonso V of Aragon, he devoted his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> to a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and ordered the noon bell for prayers during the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> in 1456. He also had <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a>'s condemnation annulled.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-callixtus-iii.jpg" alt="Pope Callixtus III" width="320" height="518" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sano di Pietro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calixtus_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Two popes, <b>Callixtus III</b> and Alexander VI of the Borgia family, came from the Kingdom of Valencia.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Hunyadi's defence of Belgrade in 1456 was celebrated throughout Europe, and the noon bell ordered by <b>Pope Callixtus III</b> to call for prayers for the Christian forces became associated with the victory.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1301-1526">Kingdom of Hungary (1301-1526) · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>A retrial authorised by <b>Pope Callixtus III</b> quashed Joan of Arc's 1431 conviction and declared her innocent.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-7">7 July in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Torreta de Canals, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=38.96,-0.59&amp;year=1430" aria-label="Torreta de Canals on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4535 767 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Pope Callixtus III"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4985 1037h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4985 1037h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=38.96,-0.59&amp;year=1430">What was here in 1430? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
